Feeling wired but tired at the end of a workday is common. Your sleep pressure is high, but your stress response is still on, so you're exhausted and keyed up at the same time.

One underrated factor is detachment. A meta-analysis of 38,124 employees linked mentally switching off from work in your free time to less fatigue and better recovery. A small end-of-day ritual can help, and so can a minute of slow breathing with longer exhales (inhale 4, exhale 6).

We wrote an evidence-based guide, including what the research doesn't support (adrenal fatigue). DeRot, coming soon to iOS, pauses your apps mid-scroll while you reset with a few calming breaths. {url}
